(collateral form of √ श्रथ्) cl. 1. P. श्लथति (only pr. p. श्लथत्), to be loose or relaxed or flaccid, BhP. :
Caus. श्लथयति id., Dhātup. xxxv, 18;
to let loose, relax, loosen, Śiś.;
to hurt, kill, W.

cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. iv, 41) श्ला॑घते (ep. also ˚ति; pf. शश्लाघे, ˚घिरे, Hariv.; Gr. also aor. अश्लाघिष्ट; fut. श्लाघिता, श्लाघिष्यते; inf. श्लाघितुम्),
to trust or confide in (dat.), ŚBr.;
to talk confidently, vaunt, boast or be proud of (instr. or loc.), Āpast.; Baudh.; MBh. &c.;
to coax, flatter, wheedle (dat.), Pāṇ. i, 4, 34, Kāś.;
to praise, commend, eulogise, celebrate, MBh.; Kāv. &c. (cf. Pāṇ.; ib.) :
Pass. श्लाघ्यते (aor. अश्लाघि), to be praised or celebrated or magnified, MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. श्लाघयति (aor. अशश्लाघत्), to encourage, comfort, console, R.;
to praise, celebrate, Hit.; BhP.
